<http://purl.org/heritagedata/schemes/mda_obj/concepts/148337> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <http://purl.org/heritagedata/schemes/mda_obj/concepts/148363> ;
    skos:inScheme <http://purl.org/heritagedata/schemes/mda_obj> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Double Handled Jar"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "A jar adapted by the addition of two handles. Handles may be horizontal or vertical loops or horizontal or curved lugs. Handles are nearly always opposed. Profiles vary and should be double indexed with the appropriate JAR type. (Source: MPRG)"@en .

<http://purl.org/heritagedata/schemes/mda_obj/concepts/148338> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <http://purl.org/heritagedata/schemes/mda_obj/concepts/96783> ;
    skos:inScheme <http://purl.org/heritagedata/schemes/mda_obj> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Bar Lug Jar"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "A distinctive form of jar being a flat-based, straight-sided or slightly rounded jar with two opposed, upright, rounded, tongue-shaped lugs raised from above the rim and bridged by added, internal struts used to suspend the pot over a fire. (Source: MPRG)"@en .

<http://purl.org/heritagedata/schemes/mda_obj/concepts/148339> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <http://purl.org/heritagedata/schemes/mda_obj/concepts/96783> ;
    skos:inScheme <http://purl.org/heritagedata/schemes/mda_obj> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Bar Lip Jar"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "A jar with one or more lips added on the outside of the vessel wall over a hole pierced through the wall. The lips do not usually rise above rim level. (Source: MPRG)"@en .

<http://purl.org/heritagedata/schemes/mda_obj/concepts/148340> a skos:Concept ;
